{"seq":null,"commit_to":{"owner":"pertson-labs","repo":"e2e-expert-repo","branch":"live/first-version--9da3f6efce10"},"doc_stem":"2026-07-26-1-e2e-overwrite-1785059446457","status":"completed","machine":{"spec_version":7,"spec_hash":"c834f46b2b0c"},"checkpoint":"navigate","run_id":"mp-eng-bc881d7d","payload":{"expand_iris":["ns__Actor_XenaGithubber","ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst"],"focus":"First version — document review submission by Xena ExpertGH","rationale":"The document is a minimal 'First version' submission by Xena ExpertGH (xena+staging@aswritten.ai). The perspective map is sparse, containing only two nodes: the actor profile for Xena Githubber (the submitter) and the Diagnostic First decision (Xena's core methodology). Both are relevant — the actor node grounds the submitter's identity and the decision node provides the methodological context for any first-version work. No other areas exist in the map to expand; there are no positions, narratives, or additional areas to surface.","n8n_execution_id":"135644","expansion_count":2,"context":"# Perspective — pertson-labs/e2e-expert-repo @ 1dc2cf0996dea4479c74039a3d2bf544377f5490\npin: 2428025f4c8cacf0539b6d3b546a9a96f3538452\n\nSections, stable-first: (1) THE MAP — the richest areas at steering grain; (2) AREA INDEX — every other area, named, one line each; (3) ACTIVE SURFACE — recent + load-bearing witnesses; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map and index never vary with your focus; your per-call material is at the end.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nDeciding where to go: each mapped area's narration tells you the SPAN of what lives under it; the area index names everything else. Expand a subtree when its narration (or name) shows your subject plausibly lives there — you'll get the trajectory, the variants, and the verbatim witness. But be strict about absence: if neither the map's narrations nor the index's names substantively cover your subject, it is NOT in this perspective — say so rather than expanding a loose thematic match (a word-overlap is not coverage). Decide from the map; expand to ground.\n\n# The map (steering grain)\n\n\n# Focus: First version — document review submission by Xena ExpertGH (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Actor_XenaGithubber, ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"2428025f4c8cacf0539b6d3b546a9a96f3538452","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":2603},"live_run_id":"9da3f6efce10","at":"2026-07-26T09:51:04Z"}
